{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be the sum of all products <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd0cb83bcbe564f348ccfd8492d244938a4d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$jk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f514e4f6a5ace002c1db61aa2478448fa82cdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq j&lt;k\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />. What is the sum of the 10 least values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/a/deaa12755d0ea5f60c1da09501c1686e89643211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 196\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 197\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 198\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 199\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/3081f1e821e51dbb8fbaa81464e1df1f85eb2767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" />, we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4fa3b5f242b59d91274c6d67849c564623e8577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1(n+1)+2(n+1)+\\cdots +n(n+1)=(1+2+\\cdots +n)(n+1)=\\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"603\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can look at the different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a57e9f3f5b0a5c034a4f76ad7e17cf2fb1d6d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ee2a54dd39409e4924b96ccc875a7516050f94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/452eae0d5fd225d3f3837715005eca308400bf54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2}\\equiv 0\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"41\" />. However, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041ed30e7f2d74d41970d1b47e6fb9907102949c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv 1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856e3e707f996835c0ac2f0d19bb6fa22dd79319.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1\\cdot {2}^2}{2}\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}.\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57ae846845fe890615194ae7162f47b1e759c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> Using the above result, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cada75d22facdbdc5f907a122fa3c67833af1a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_5\\equiv 1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a3fd82bedcbf8d8fe475d9d82fbd04d7ca1c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449f9443326f9b0e025114ef8c22b60bb9955459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/20838b5ca8856f98e9825f2c50e2e21733d63274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> are all divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/57479e2729ec45042b4ed5e73d9974b88d288922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 3=9$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/a/15aaa8911c0bf4c6d8915d5c6e9e9f7e6722940d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3827e0e647e235f93d88b08435f715a045be20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750d22bf18ad4e54bf9db0c4cd748d85acec1e43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> all divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f221aad24107fb95385d7fd52651aebe8a3ee22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{26}, S_{27}, S_{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d4ead07a6208fc243b0a75e2fcbd6125d213f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041f005125a0cff7b8a9977268b8daef38b76777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+9+10+17+18+19+26+27+28+35=27+54+81+35=162+35=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 197} .$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"721\" height=\"32\" /> -BorealBear\n</p><p>-minor edit by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Yiyj1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Yiyj1 (page does not exist)\">Yiyj1</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(bash)\">Solution 2 (bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we have a wonky function, we start by trying out some small cases and see what happens. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then there is one case. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for this case. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b117557f5fcee6f4f7e9bc93ed419e80b578dc05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 3 + 2 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" /> which is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76204e22ad08f090992d0962c2e61c377d76c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 4 + 2 \\cdot 4 + 3 \\cdot 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" /> which is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that we are still at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If we try a few more cases, we find that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we are adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore, we are still at a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c60d660fa657c672598b60a72ebef8fbb67f716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10(1+2+3+...+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we have another multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So, every time we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we always have a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Think about it: When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it will have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c7900f590ae8a94906dfb3f2c0cece08a9e7e947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />, so it is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, our numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe499fd85f3ce652f01e2dcd3a26eb2dde45612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8, 9, 10, 17, 18, 19, 26, 27, 28, 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"17\" />. Adding the numbers up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17aef266a70a4ea5360b6b6a9d5178b3dd6ecacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) 197}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"77\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924c65b93da7c8032dc57b51163bc1168d479181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n, &lt;} = \\left\\{ \\left( j , k \\right) : 1 \\leq j &lt; k \\leq n \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648afcb384236b386c70c531a22977498b7506e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n, &gt;} = \\left\\{ \\left( j , k \\right) : 1 \\leq k &lt; j \\leq n \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f569e5cc7f318cc2ad3814b6ee4821b0b1271a27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n, =} = \\left\\{ \\left( j , k \\right) : 1 \\leq j = k \\leq n \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0a6224ac28b8e50308157352f06f248138b13d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\left( j , k \\right) \\in A_{n,&lt;}} jk = \\sum_{\\left( j , k \\right) \\in A_{n,&gt;}} jk = S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"248\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c881e2c45ca7f01026dc346bf40163f7efd39b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} S_n &amp; = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\sum_{\\left( j , k \\right) \\in A_{n,&lt;}} jk = \\sum_{\\left( j , k \\right) \\in A_{n,&gt;}} jk \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\sum_{1 \\leq j, k \\leq n} jk - {\\left( j , k \\right) \\in A_{n,=}} jk \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{k=1}^n jk - \\sum_{j=1}^n j^2 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{n^2 \\left( n + 1 \\right)^2}{4} - \\frac{n \\left( n + 1 \\right) \\left( 2 n + 1 \\right) }{6} \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right) \\left( 3 n + 2 \\right)}{24} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"338\" height=\"294\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is divisible by 3 if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb6dd605db26142384051d785ea19f0cd77f786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right) \\left( 3 n + 2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7ca87ca33a3c6391aaa64aee3ef7c578f6c5e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\cdot 3 = 8 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb6dd605db26142384051d785ea19f0cd77f786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right) \\left( 3 n + 2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" /> is always divisible by 8. Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is not even an integer.\n</p><p>Second, we find conditions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb6dd605db26142384051d785ea19f0cd77f786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right) \\left( 3 n + 2 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by 9.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/4205cef6ca15bbfdad55c3a83fd2d18e76814466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> is not divisible by 3, it cannot be divisible by 9.\n</p><p>Hence, we need to find conditions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877b5a83a0c4c83c0fbda513f086de263e8af209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by 9.\nThis holds of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81aaa4dce03b2884f84bec4ca2ff9fa12d3a5306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 0, \\pm 1 \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the 10 least values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877b5a83a0c4c83c0fbda513f086de263e8af209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( n - 1 \\right) n \\left( n + 1 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by 9 (equivalently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is divisible by 3) are 8, 9, 10, 17, 18, 19, 26, 27, 28, 35.\nTheir sum is 197.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1ae62e25a0a49b8fa87982e70c0721df1000ad05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }197}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_PDIrta6r8s\">https://youtu.be/_PDIrta6r8s</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution 2 by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/M8tF1uSOfXA\">https://youtu.be/M8tF1uSOfXA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B\">2021 Fall AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015128\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 628/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2474/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 308/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19645/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.101      1 -total\n 59.86%    8.441      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.26%    5.536      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22201:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015128 and revision id 203025. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}